The status-read endpoint and persistence mechanism are intentionally not invented here. An absent result can be inconclusive if indexing or replication is delayed. The service contract determines whether and when another write is safe.

If the approved client already retries requests, account for that behavior before enabling order submission. Local button guards and a stable request identifier alone do not establish server-side idempotency across restarts, devices, or new feature instances.

## 8. Verify before connecting production traffic

| Controlled test | Expected result |
|---|---|
| Qualifying failures reach the threshold | Circuit opens. |
| Request arrives while open | Injected operation is not invoked. |
| Cooldown expires | One recovery probe is admitted when a caller arrives. |
| Competing half-open requests | Additional probes are rejected. |
| Probe succeeds / fails | Circuit closes / reopens according to the defined policy. |
| Probe is cancelled | Permit is released and circuit reopens without counting cancellation as an outage. |
| Earlier attempt completes after a newer circuit generation | It does not overwrite newer breaker state. |
| Invalid configuration | Construction fails instead of silently using unsafe defaults. |
| Order response is lost | Unknown state; no automatic duplicate order. |

Use an injected clock and scripted operations, not live outages or real orders. Cover transport cancellation, classification, retry ownership, and session recovery through the actual application's tests. The production-code coverage requirement and platform test commands belong in Testing & Quality.

