## 4. Keep account and order ownership safe

| Event | Required behavior |
|---|---|
| Account targeting is introduced | Confirm context, cache partitioning, and activation rules for the pinned SDK. Do not add it to the application-wide sample unchanged. |
| Account switch or logout | Hide old targeted decisions, invalidate prior work, and reject late updates until the correct scope is verified. |
| Flag changes while quantity is being edited | Apply the documented activation boundary. Recheck before starting a new write. |
| Flag changes after submission | Preserve submission/reconciliation state; do not cancel recovery or fabricate failure. |
| Remote service is unreachable | Use only the approved default/stale policy. A client flag alone is not an immediate emergency stop. |

Server authorization is always required. An offline device may continue to hold older flag values; enforce high-risk shutdown rules on the backend when immediate enforcement is required.

